{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>All the words of HaShem which He had sent him.</b> This includes the vision that he saw in the bush, and also the matter of the mission, which he had been resisting." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'All the words of HaShem' — the Rabbis say: He revealed to him the secret of the Explicit Name. The intent of this Midrash is that Moses told Aaron the Names that the Holy One, blessed be He, had made known to him above, and they are אהיה אשר אהיה, whose meaning is the attribute of judgment within the attribute of mercy. And he made known to him that the Name אהיה and the special Name (the Tetragrammaton) are all one. And He revealed to him that the Name אדני emerges from them: אלף from אהיה, and י from יהוה at the end, and the attribute of judgment in the middle, as it says, ״כי שמי בקרבו״ (Exodus 23:21). And so he explained to them that אהיה אשר אהיה means the attribute of judgment within the attribute of mercy, which I have already mentioned above, and this is the view of the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:16.047728558Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}